    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `ageBand` derivation feature. When a create request includes `birthDate` (ISO date), the owner's response now carries an `ageBand` of `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+), computed as the age at `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges, following the existing Spring/MapStruct/OpenAPI-generated-DTO conventions:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (optional, `format: date`) to the editable `OwnerFields` schema, and `ageBand` (read-only enum `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `birthDate` `LocalDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct's `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` auto-maps it from the request by name.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `ageBand(owner)` derivation method and wired it into `toOwnerDto` via `@Mapping`. It uses `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` and returns `null` when `birthDate` (or `registrationDate`) is absent.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column. The hsqldb schema is the one the test suite actually uses (`ddl-auto=none`), so this was required for the column to exist; the others were updated for parity.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreDerivesAgeBand` (creates an owner with `birthDate=1990-01-01` and expects `ageBand=ADULT`) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
